  "dcterms:title": "TSAR - Tracking System for Alternative methods towards Regulatory acceptance",
  "dcterms:description": "A BioBricks brick named 'tsar' identifying it with the TSAR (Tracking System for Alternative methods towards Regulatory acceptance) database of the European Commission Joint Research Centre (JRC). Per the brick README the source is https://tsar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/. TSAR tracks the development, validation and regulatory acceptance status of alternative (non-animal) test methods. The on-disk brick contains only a README and an MIT LICENSE for the brick tooling (not the data), so the packaged data files cannot be confirmed from the repository; the sibling brick tsar-jrc-toxicity-data downloads the TSAR CSV export.",
